============================================================
  HUMAN FINDINGS GATE
============================================================

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  SUMMARY
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The bug hypothesis was confirmed: preempted requests double-counted their decode tokens in TotalOutputTokens, inflating the metric by 9.1% (114,630 vs ground truth 105,082) when 265 preemptions occurred. The three-line fix eliminates the inflation exactly, and a negative-control arm verified the fix is a no-op when no preemptions occur.

  * CONFIRMED (h-main): After the fix, the small-cache run (--total-kv-blocks 600, 265 preemptions) reports total_output_tokens=105,082, exactly matching the no-preemption ground truth. Before the fix it reported 114,630 — a 9.1% inflation.
  * CONFIRMED (h-control-negative): The large-cache run (--total-kv-blocks 60000, 0 preemptions) produces byte-identical output with and without the fix, confirming no side effects in the zero-preemption path.
  * Root cause: scheduleBatch in sim/simulator.go incremented PreemptionCount but never subtracted already-counted output tokens when a request was preempted and re-queued. The fix computes OutputTokensLost = max(0, ProgressIndex − len(InputTokens)) before resetting ProgressIndex, then subtracts it from TotalOutputTokens.
  * A new regression test (TestPreemption_TotalOutputTokens_NoDoubleCount) exercises the invariant at unit-test scale with 47 preemptions and passes.
  * No surprises: both arms matched predictions exactly, and no uncommitted files remain in the worktree.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

